An algorithm is a step-by-step sequence of well-defined instructions designed to solve a specific problem or perform a task.
Algorithms can be represented in Pseudocode or Flowcharts.
Pseudocode: A high-level code-like representation that uses programming constructs (like INPUT, OUTPUT, IF-ELSE) without strict language syntax.
Flowcharts: A visual representation of the flow of the program using standardized symbols.
Example problem:
  Algorithm:-
    Step 1: Start.
    Step 2: Read/Input the values of Basic Salary, HRA (House Rent Allowance), and DA (Dearness Allowance)
    Step 3: Calculate Gross Salary by adding Basic Salary, HRA, and DA.
    Step 4: Display/Print the calculated Gross Salary.
    Step 5: Stop.
  Pseudocode:-
    BEGIN
      READ basic_salary, hra, da
      gross_salary = basic_salary + hra + da
      PRINT gross_salary
    END
  FlowChart:-
    Oval(START) -> ||gm(INPUT basic_salary, hra, da) -> Rectangle(gross_salary = basic_salary + hra + da) -> ||gm(PRINT gross_salary) -> Oval(STOP)

